reply:
Here's the TypeScript version, with the argument types of the original function preserved:

```typescript
export function debounce<T extends (...args: any[]) => void>(
  fn: T,
  wait: number,
): (...args: Parameters<T>) => void {
  let timer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined;
  return function (this: ThisParameterType<T>, ...args: Parameters<T>) {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    timer = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), wait);
  };
}
```

Usage:

```typescript
const onResize = debounce((width: number) => console.log(width), 200);
onResize(1024);   // ✅
onResize("wide"); // ❌ type error
```

`ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>` keeps it working in both the browser and Node, where timers have different types.

